<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42312" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρεσ-χηλέω</span></b>  (freq. with v.l.
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρεσ-χελέω</span></b> ), used only in
			pres., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>talk
				lightly, to be jocular,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παίζειν καὶ ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					545e
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Lg.</u>
				885c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>DMort.</u>
				16.3
			</span></i>, etc.: c. inf., <i>discuss jocularly
				whether..,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>VA</u>
				2.14
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> trans.,
				<i>quiz, banter,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινα</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				236b
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τι</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				6.223e
			</span></i>, etc.; <i>tease, worry,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				3.37
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				15.22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Musc.Enc.</u>
				10
			</span></i>: c. dat. pers., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ λόγος ἐ. νῷν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phlb.</u>
					53e
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. acc. cogn.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προφάσεις, πολέμου ἀφορμάς ἐ.,</span>
			<i>find trifling</i> excuses or occasions, <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>Pun.</u>
				74
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Mith.</u>
				64
			</span></i> ; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρίσχηλος.</span></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
